# Jaguar E-type Series 1 4.2 fixed-head coupe, 1964-1968.
#
# The 4.2-litre Series 1: the same body as the 3.8 with a larger engine, a
# stronger gearbox and revised brakes. The fixed-head coupe is modelled.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jaguar_E-Type
#
# Dimensions 4.453 x 1.657 x 1.222 m, wheelbase 2.438 m (same shell as the 3.8).
#
# Shape reference: a true level side elevation of a red FHC, plus front and
# rear three-quarters and a detail. The side car is identified as a 4.2 by its
# uploader's title only; the front car carries the definitive E-TYPE JAGUAR 4.2
# boot badge. The limitation is recorded.
#
# Colours: grade (d); no period UK document was sighted. Cream, Carmen Red,
# Black and British Racing Green are period Jaguar names recorded as context.
# Weights 6, 4, 3, 3, total 16, provisional pending the central rebase.
#
# Speed 245 km/h. Comfort 62/423, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 62. Classes 3,4.
# Dates October 1964 to 1968 production, road tail staggered 1979-1981.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/jaguar-e-type-s1-42.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/jaguar-e-type-s1-42.dae. References:
# citycars/references/jaguar-e-type-s1-42/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: built as a variant of the Series 1 3.8 master. The side
# car is identified as a 4.2 by its uploader's title only; the front car carries
# the definitive 4.2 boot badge. Wire-wheel, lamp and badge detail is simplified.


obj=citycar
